{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqhdjggg6h1","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","title":"pluggable LLM backend merged to main","summary":"The pluggable LLM backend feature merged to main at 429750c on 2026-06-16 (feature orch/feature/pluggable-backend, 12 files, +2744/-123; five layers each single-attempt code-judged + tier-1 merged before the gated feature->main promotion). Delivers: a provider adapter seam in lib/llm-backend.js — a registry (registerProvider/getProvider/listProviders) + getActiveBackend(overlay) reading overlay.config.backend {provider, model}, defaulting to Claude. Providers: Claude, Codex, Cursor are kind agentic-cli (they SPAWN a local CLI child process); OpenRouter is kind api and runs IN-PROCESS over Node https with NO child process — this is the antivirus-clean path that sidesteps the Kaspersky hidden-child-process interception. Config surface: GET/POST /config/backend (routes/config.js) reads/sets the active backend; the daemon /config auth gate was widened to startsWith('/config') so POST stays write-protected. Dashboard: a backend selector lives in the settings popup of public/graph.html (pure logic in lib/backend-ui.js) showing per-provider isAvailable/isAuthed badges and a local-CLI antivirus-awareness notice gated to agentic-cli kind (offers an AV exclusion OR switching to the API backend). The headless judge drain in lib/headless-drain.js routes through getActiveBackend().buildInvocation for agentic-cli, calls the in-process runJudgeLoop for api, and hard-blocks with skip:no_backend when no valid backend. Safety unchanged: ORCH_HEADLESS_DRAINS still default-OFF, backend defaults to Claude, fire-rate backoff + per-tick cap intact. To use a non-Claude backend: select it in the dashboard settings; for OpenRouter set env OPENROUTER_API_KEY (or OPENROUTER_KEY), or per-provider bin overrides CODEX_BIN/CURSOR_BIN for the local CLIs.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-17T01:10:18.640Z","vec":[-0.061490342020988464,-0.008614961989223957,-0.1126